        <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
          <p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇬🇷</strong> <strong>Greece - Upholds Neo Nazi’s conviction. </strong>A Greek appeals court has upheld the 2020 convictions of leaders and members of the neo-Nazi party Golden Dawn. It confirmed that the party operated as a criminal organization. The ruling reaffirmed sentences for 42 figures, including former leader Nikos Michaloliakos (<a href="https://www.dw.com/en/greece-athens-golden-dawn-party-convictions/a-76218570" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">request denied</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇻🇪 Venezuela - Gold agreement with the US. </strong>Venezuela’s state mining company, Minerven, has signed a multimillion-dollar agreement to sell 650 to 1,000 kilograms of gold to Trafigura. This gold will be refined in the US. The agreement happened during US Interior Secretary Doug Burgum’s visit. It is the third major resource agreement under the Trump administration (<a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/international-business/venezuela-to-supply-up-to-1000-kg-of-gold-to-us-sources-say-deal-more-beneficial-for-caracas/articleshow/129080467.cms" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">digging for gold</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇩🇪 Germany - Hefty sentence for stabbing</strong>. A Berlin court sentenced a 20-year-old Syrian man to 13 years for stabbing a Spanish tourist at the Holocaust memorial in February 2025. Prosecutors said he acted for IS and targeted a Jewish person. He was tried as an adult because of his maturity. The attack happened just days before Germany’s elections, sparking debates about Syrian refugees and migration (<a href="https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-holocaust-memorial-attacker-given-13-years-in-prison/a-76224858" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">justice served)</a>.
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇸🇳 Senegal - ECOWAS tackles jihad. </strong>West African states plan to create a 2,000-strong force to fight jihadist threats. This force does not include Burkina Faso, Mali, and Niger, as they have left ECOWAS after recent coups. Troops will stay in their home countries, with Sierra Leone acting as a logistical hub. Talks about funding and deployment are ongoing (<a href="https://www.taipeitimes.com/News/world/archives/2026/03/05/2003853307" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">West African cooperation</a>).
</p>
<p
  style="
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-top: 0px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  "
>
  <strong>🇫🇮 Finland - Lifts ban on hosting nuclear weapons. </strong>Finland plans to lift its ban on nuclear weapons. This change aims to align better with NATO’s deterrence strategy. The proposal will amend the 1987 Nuclear Energy bill. It allows nuclear weapons for national defense. Defence Minister Antti Häkkänen stated that this move addresses security concerns following Russia's invasion of Ukraine (<a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c14m5llnrlpo" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #06266d; color: black;">change in course</a>).
</p>
        </mj-text>
